  "scenario_narratives": {
    "base": "Quest keeps compounding as the national consolidator of hospital outreach labs: FY2026 lands ~+7.5% on acquired books, then growth settles at 4-5% (2-3% organic volume/mix, 1-2pp tuck-ins) fading to 3%. PAMA Medicare clinical-lab-fee cuts are either delayed again or absorbed (Medicare CLFS is a mid-single-digit share of revenue). Invigorate automation and AI-driven revenue-cycle savings (~3%/yr of cost base) roughly offset wage inflation, so pre-SBC EBITDA margin creeps from 20.1% to 21%. Capex stays elevated near 4.5% of revenue as labs are automated.",
    "bull": "Advanced diagnostics (brain health/AD blood tests, oncology MRD, consumer-initiated testing) and a steady cadence of health-system outreach deals push growth to 6-8% for three years; PAMA is permanently reformed (SALSA-style) removing the reimbursement overhang; automation drives margin back toward the ~22-23% pre-COVID-peak range. Buybacks and a 3%+ dividend continue, with leverage staying ~2.5x.",
    "bear": "PAMA cuts of up to 15% per code finally take effect in 2027 and commercial payers follow Medicare's lead, Labcorp and hospital systems compete harder on price for outreach books, and wage/courier costs outrun productivity. Growth collapses to ~2% after the FY2026 acquisition lift and pre-SBC EBITDA margin falls to 18.5% (the FY2023-24 trough level). Terminal multiple compressed to 12x for an ex-growth, price-taker lab."
  },
  "valuation_philosophy": {
    "summary": "Quest is a mature, cash-generative US clinical lab consolidator. Value rests on durable volumes and a measured margin creep rather than growth; owner FCF charges SBC and award-withholding taxes, holds the share count flat, and deducts net debt and capitalised NCI. Reimbursement policy is the dominant swing factor, carried by the 25% bear weight rather than a WACC premium.",
    "key_risks_to_valuation": [
      "PAMA / Medicare Clinical Lab Fee Schedule cuts (deferred repeatedly; could bite from 2027)",
      "Commercial payer rate pressure and utilisation-management denials",
      "Competition from Labcorp and hospital systems for outreach lab books; acquisition price inflation",
      "Wage and logistics inflation outrunning automation savings",
      "Leverage (~2.4x net debt/EBITDA) constrains buybacks if M&A continues",
      "Cyber/IT incidents (2019 AMCA billing-vendor breach precedent)"
    ]
  },
