    "notes": "MODEL: owner-FCF component DCF (dcf-methods routing row 1: US operating company - clinical laboratory testing services, ~$11B revenue, stable margins; not a bank/REIT/holdco). First valuation of DGX (no MEMORY entry). Horizon 10 years. EBITDA is built PRE-SBC (FY2025 GAAP EBITDA $2,126M = operating income $1,556M + D&A $570M, + SBC $88M = $2,214M, 20.1% of revenue; H1 2026 20.1%) so SBC is charged exactly once in the flows. D&A includes acquired-intangible amortisation (tax deductible for asset deals), so D&A% glides down toward capex% by the terminal year to avoid perpetuating an amortisation tax shield. Cash tax: FY2025 cash taxes $169M were depressed by 2025 US tax law restoring 100% bonus depreciation and domestic R&D expensing (FY2023 $317M, FY2024 $256M); the unlevered rate ramps 21% -> 24%. Working capital: receivables-heavy business (payer billing), so growth consumes cash - negative capture on the revenue change (-6%: receivables ~12% of revenue less payables/accruals ~6%). Terminal caps: 15x base (structurally slow grower; Gordon at 7.5%/2.5% would be 20.5x), 17x bull, 12x bear. Price is a regular-session close, not an after-hours print. Guidance: no filing text was extracted for this XBRL-only build; FY2026 year-1 growth is anchored to H1 2026 revenue +9.7% YoY (acquired outreach books incl. Fresenius/Spectra, Corewell, LifeLabs lapping) moderating in H2 to ~+7.5% for the year. Buybacks are real (FY2021-25 cumulative $4.5B), so the flat count is funded, not a convention.",
